# LangGraph Reference (TypeScript)

**Trigger**: Reference material for LangGraph.js TypeScript implementation. Read when building new agents, debugging graph issues, or verifying agent structure.

> **Note**: LangGraph.js is aspirational — not yet implemented in this project. This reference serves as the guide for when the agent layer is built.

> **Core patterns**: See [langgraph-patterns.mdc](.cursor/rules/langgraph-patterns.mdc) for state design, node purity, tool loops, routing, and interrupts.

> **Skill**: See [langgraph-orchestration SKILL.md](.cursor/skills/langgraph-orchestration/SKILL.md) for full workflow examples (signal analysis, cross-signal inference, article generation).

## Checkpointer Setup

Use `PostgresSaver` from `@langchain/langgraph-checkpoint-postgres`. Reuses the existing `DATABASE_URL`. Never use `MemorySaver` in production.

```typescript
import { PostgresSaver } from "@langchain/langgraph-checkpoint-postgres";
import { DATABASE_URL } from "@/lib/config";

export async function getCheckpointer(): Promise<PostgresSaver> {
  return PostgresSaver.fromConnString(DATABASE_URL);
}
```

### Checkpointer Rules

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Lazy init | Create once per process, cache the instance |
| Call `setup()` once | Only on first creation (creates tables) |
| Thread isolation | Each user session gets a unique `threadId` |
| No manual DB writes in nodes | Let the checkpointer handle persistence |
| Connection pooling | `PostgresSaver` manages its own pool |

### Graph Compilation with Checkpointer

```typescript
import { StateGraph, START, END } from "@langchain/langgraph";
import { getCheckpointer } from "./checkpointer";

export async function buildGraph() {
  const checkpointer = await getCheckpointer();
  
  const graph = new StateGraph<SignalAnalysisState>({
    channels: {
      // ... state schema
    },
  });
  
  graph.addNode("extractFacts", extractFacts);
  graph.addNode("classify", classifySentiment);
  graph.addEdge(START, "extractFacts");
  graph.addEdge("extractFacts", "classify");
  graph.addEdge("classify", END);
  
  return graph.compile({ checkpointer });
}
```

