## State Definition

Use TypeScript interfaces with explicit field types. Every list field needs a reducer pattern.

```typescript
// src/lib/agent/types.ts
import { BaseMessage } from "@langchain/core/messages";

interface SignalAnalysisState {
  signalId: string;
  rawText: string;
  companyId: string;
  facts: Array<{ text: string; confidence: number }>;
  sentiment: "POSITIVE" | "NEGATIVE" | "NEUTRAL";
  confidenceScore: number;
  summary: string;
  error?: string;
  messages: BaseMessage[];
}
```

### Reducer Selection

| Pattern | Implementation | Use Case |
|---------|----------------|----------|
| Replace value | Direct assignment (last-write-wins) | `sentiment`, `confidenceScore`, `error` |
| Append list | Spread operator or concat | `facts`, `patterns`, `signalTexts` |
| Messages | Built-in message reducer | Chat history (built-in dedup + ordering) |

