## ToolNode from @langchain/langgraph/prebuilt

Use `ToolNode` for explicit tool execution loops. Never handle tool calls inside model nodes.

```typescript
import { ToolNode } from "@langchain/langgraph/prebuilt";
import { ChatOpenAI } from "@langchain/openai";
import { searchTool, scrapeTool } from "./tools";

const tools = [searchTool, scrapeTool];
const llm = new ChatOpenAI({ model: "gpt-4o" }).bindTools(tools);

async function modelNode(state: SignalAnalysisState) {
  const response = await llm.invoke(state.messages);
  return { messages: [response] };
}

const toolNode = new ToolNode(tools);

graph.addNode("model", modelNode);
graph.addNode("tools", toolNode);
graph.addConditionalEdges("model", shouldCallTools, {
  tools: "tools",
  end: END,
});
graph.addEdge("tools", "model"); // loop back to model after tool execution
```

### ToolNode Rules

| Rule | Detail |
|------|--------|
| Explicit loop | Model → conditional → ToolNode → model |
| Never hide tool calls | Graph must see every tool invocation |
| Bind tools to LLM | `llm.bindTools([tools])` before model node |
| Tool-loop guard | Add iteration counter to prevent infinite loops |

