## Anti-Patterns

| Anti-Pattern | Why It's Bad | Fix |
|---|---|---|
| **State mutation in nodes** | Breaks reducer merge, corrupts checkpoints | Return partial state objects: `return { facts: [...] }` |
| **Hidden tool calls in model nodes** | Graph can't track or replay tool execution | Use `ToolNode` + conditional edge + loop-back |
| **Unbounded loops** | Infinite loops burn tokens and crash | Add `iteration` field + `MAX_ITERATIONS` guard |
| **Blocking I/O in async nodes** | Blocks the event loop, kills concurrency | Use native `fetch()`, Prisma — no blocking calls |
| **Missing checkpointing** | No crash recovery, lost progress on failure | Always `compile({ checkpointer })` in production |
| **Side effects in routing functions** | Non-deterministic routing, breaks replay | Pure inspection only — read state, return string |
| **Manual DB writes + checkpointer** | Double-write, inconsistent state on replay | Use checkpointer for all graph persistence |
| **God nodes** | Multiple responsibilities, hard to test | Split into focused single-purpose nodes |
| **`MemorySaver` in production** | Lost on restart, no crash recovery | Use `PostgresSaver` with `DATABASE_URL` |
| **Sync I/O in async nodes** | Blocks event loop | Use `await` for all I/O |

