## Verification Checklist

Before committing TypeScript LangGraph code:

- [ ] State uses TypeScript interfaces with explicit field types
- [ ] All nodes are `async` functions and return partial state objects
- [ ] All routing functions are pure (no mutation, no side effects, no LLM calls)
- [ ] Tool-enabled steps use `ToolNode` + conditional edge + loop-back edge
- [ ] Tool-loop guards present with `iteration` field + `MAX_ITERATIONS`
- [ ] Graph compiled with `checkpointer: PostgresSaver` (not `MemorySaver`)
- [ ] All I/O is async (`fetch`, Prisma) — no blocking calls
- [ ] No manual DB writes in node functions (use checkpointer)
- [ ] Thread config uses unique `threadId` per session
- [ ] Error paths route to dead-letter nodes, not silent drops
- [ ] Interrupts used for human-in-the-loop on high-confidence decisions
- [ ] Streaming uses `streamEvents({ version: "v2" })` for token-level output
